  data: {
    LLM: '1. Turn order: discard (compulsory) â†’ play combinations (optional) â†’ draw (compulsory). 2. Draw: one from closed pile OR any number from discard pile (if at least one drawn card is immediately played). 3. Combinations: sequences (3+ consecutive same suit; max 3 jokers, min 1 natural); groups of 3+ Threes or 3+ Aces (no jokers). 4. Printed jokers can be replaced by natural cards and reused; sliding jokers (Twos) stay in sequence when replaced, slid to one end. 5. To declare show: team must have 5+ complete sets, at least one pure (no jokers). Wrong show = 0 for declaring team. 6. Ground show: when draw pile empties, player may declare or draw from discard and play one turn.',
    Player: '1. Turn order: discard (compulsory) â†’ play combinations (optional) â†’ draw (compulsory). 2. Draw: one from closed pile OR any number from discard pile (if at least one drawn card is immediately played). 3. Combinations: sequences (3+ consecutive same suit; max 3 jokers, min 1 natural); groups of 3+ Threes or 3+ Aces (no jokers). 4. Printed jokers can be replaced by natural cards and reused; sliding jokers (Twos) stay in sequence when replaced, slid to one end. 5. To declare show: team must have 5+ complete sets, at least one pure (no jokers). Wrong show = 0 for declaring team. 6. Ground show: when draw pile empties, player may declare or draw from discard and play one turn.',
    objective: 'First team to reach 1,500 points (4-deck standard). Score from cards on table, opponent unplayed cards, complete-set bonuses, suited-group bonuses, and show bonus.',
    gameplay: '1. Turn order: discard (compulsory) â†’ play combinations (optional) â†’ draw (compulsory). 2. Draw: one from closed pile OR any number from discard pile (if at least one drawn card is immediately played). 3. Combinations: sequences (3+ consecutive same suit; max 3 jokers, min 1 natural); groups of 3+ Threes or 3+ Aces (no jokers). 4. Printed jokers can be replaced by natural cards and reused; sliding jokers (Twos) stay in sequence when replaced, slid to one end. 5. To declare show: team must have 5+ complete sets, at least one pure (no jokers). Wrong show = 0 for declaring team. 6. Ground show: when draw pile empties, player may declare or draw from discard and play one turn.',
